{
  "_": [
    "Fixtures for scripts/authz-support.php — the authorization matrix.",
    "",
    "Keyed by ROUTE PATTERN PREFIX, never by placeholder name alone: {id} is a",
    "member on /members/{id} and a discussion group on /groups/{id}, and a single",
    "global value for {id} would hide that. Each key ends at its own first",
    "placeholder, so no two keys can both prefix the same route and the longest",
    "match is always the only match.",
    "",
    "THE VALUES NEED ONLY BE WELL-FORMED, NOT REAL. RbacGuard runs before the",
    "controller (ARCHITECTURE.md 12), so a route answers the authorization",
    "question identically whether the row exists or not: refused is refused, and",
    "a 404 for a row that is not there still means the caller got past the guard.",
    "Ids are therefore 1, and tokens are the right shape rather than a real one.",
    "",
    "A route whose prefix is absent from this file FAILS the matrix rather than",
    "being skipped. Tests\\Security\\AuthorizationMatrixInventoryTest enforces that",
    "on every commit, so a new route arrives with its fixture or not at all — a",
    "matrix that silently shrinks would keep reporting no finding while covering",
    "less and less."
  ],
